```latex
A large number of pages are located on the disk in the computer. The computer receives a stream of requests for different pages. To allow fast access to the pages, we have a cache memory of size \( n \) pages in which we store the most recent pages, i.e., those requested recently (LRU model). Example: \( n = 4 \). After the request stream 6, 5, 9, 4, 5, 4, 7 the cache will contain the pages 7, 4, 5, 9 where 7 is the freshest and 9 is the stalest. If the next request is for page 3, then 9 will be removed from the cache.

\begin{enumerate}
