```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{amsmath}

\begin{document}
We find the median of the array and count how many times it appears in $O(n)$ time. If it appears at least $n/k$ times, we return it. Otherwise, we proceed recursively with the two subarrays—one to the right of the median and one to the left. In step $i$, the size of the array is $\left\lfloor \frac{n}{2^i} \right\rfloor$, so we will definitely stop when $2^i = k$. The total running time is $O(n\log k)$: the running time of each step is $O(n)$ and there are at most $\log k$ steps.
\end{document}
```

