```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}

\title{Data Structure Description}
\author{}
\date{}

\begin{document}

\maketitle

\section*{Description of the Data Structures Used for Implementation (and Purpose of Each Data Structure):}

Three data structures need to be maintained. One to hold the board, one to hold the contents of the columns, and one to hold the contents of the rows. When I mention a matrix, it refers to a two-dimensional array of size $n \times n$. 

For the board, we maintain a matrix \(A\) such that the content of the board at position \(i,j\) is \(A[i,j]\), and 0 indicates that the cell is empty. For the row contents, we maintain a matrix \(B\) such that if \texttt{num} appears in row \(i\), then \(B[i,\texttt{num}] = 1\); otherwise, 0. For the column contents, we maintain a matrix \(C\) such that if \texttt{num} appears in column \(j\), then \(C[j,\texttt{num}] = 1\); otherwise, 0.

\section*{Description of the Actions:}

\subsection*{Contains(\(i,j\))}
If \(A[i,j] \neq 0\), return \(A[i,j]\).

\subsection*{Write}
If \(B[i,\texttt{num}] = 0\) and \(C[j,\texttt{num}] = 0\), perform the assignments: \(C[j,\texttt{num}] = 1\), \(B[i,\texttt{num}] = 1\), and \(A[i,j] = \texttt{num}\). Otherwise, return that the action is illegal.

\subsection*{Erase}
Preserve the value \(A[i,j] = \texttt{num}\) and perform the assignments \(B[i,\texttt{num}] = 0\), \(C[j,\texttt{num}] = 0\), and \(A[i,j] = 0\).

\section*{Time and Space Complexity:}

The initialization is \(O(n^2)\) due to the allocation of 3 two-dimensional arrays. The complexity for each operation is constant since there is a fixed number of array accesses.

\end{document}
```

