\begin{quote}
In the following section, the initialization time and space complexity is O(1), and the space complexity at any given moment is O of the number of elements in the data structure. Describe how a vector of length m can be represented to support insertion at position i, reading from position i, and deletion at position i in O(\log m) worst-case time for each operation.
\end{quote}

answer_translation_latex:
\textbf{Central Data Structure:} AVL Tree. \textbf{Brief Description:}
The key will be the pair (i,j) where the comparison between keys will be lexicographic (compare i, and if there is a tie, compare j).
The value will be the content of the matrix at position (i,j).

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}

\begin{document}

\section*{Description of Data Structures for Implementation (and Purpose of Each Data Structure):}

The same solution as in (a), using the data structure in section (c) instead of the two-dimensional arrays.

\section*{Description of the Data Structures Used for Implementation (and Purpose of Each Data Structure):}

We need to maintain 3 data structures. One to hold the board, one to hold the contents of the columns, and one to hold the contents of the rows. We will use three AVL trees where the key will be the pair $(i,j)$, and the comparison between keys will be lexicographic (compare $i$, and if there is a tie, compare $j$).

The value will be the content of the matrix at position $(i,j)$. Each such AVL tree represents a matrix supporting operations of insertion, reading, and deletion in $O(\log m)$ time. From now on, we will refer to this structure as a matrix.

\begin{itemize}
    \item For the board – we will maintain a matrix $A$ such that the content of the board at position $i,j$ is $A[i,j]$, and $0$ indicates that the cell is empty.
    \item For the contents of the rows – we will maintain a matrix $B$ such that if \texttt{num} appears in row $i$, then $B[i,\texttt{num}] = 1$; otherwise, $0$.
    \item For the contents of the columns – we will maintain a matrix $C$ such that if \texttt{num} appears in column $j$, then $C[j,\texttt{num}] = 1$; otherwise, $0$.
\end{itemize}

\section*{Description of Operations:}

\begin{itemize}
    \item \texttt{Contains(i,j):} If $A[i,j] \neq 0$, return $A[i,j]$.
    \item \texttt{Write:} If $B[i,\texttt{num}] = 0$ and $C[j,\texttt{num}] = 0$, perform the assignments $C[j,\texttt{num}] = 1$, $B[i,\texttt{num}] = 1$, and $A[i,j] = 1$. Otherwise, return that the operation is illegal.
    \item \texttt{Erase:} Store $A[i,j] = \texttt{num}$ and perform the assignments $B[i,\texttt{num}] = C[j,\texttt{num}] = A[i,j] = 0$.
\end{itemize}

\section*{Time and Space Complexity:}

The initialization requires $O(n^2)$ due to the allocation of 3 two-dimensional arrays. Each operation has constant complexity because there is a fixed number of array accesses.

\end{document}
```

