Define a zig-zag array, for which there exist $1 \leq j \leq i \leq n$ such that all elements in the array from 1 to $i$ are in increasing order, all elements from $i$ to $j$ are in decreasing order, and all elements from $j$ to $n$ are in increasing order. We will call $i$ the peak element and $j$ the valley element.

For each problem, provide an upper and lower bound and prove them.

\textbf{Problem A} - Input: Array. Output: Returns TRUE if and only if the array is a zig-zag array.

\textbf{Problem B} - Input: Zig-zag array and location of the valley element. Output: Location of the peak element.

\textbf{Problem C} - Input: Zig-zag array. Output: Location of the peak element and the valley element.

\end{document}
```

